Rendering audio for 1 card in deck.txt
FlashTerm: --generate-audio needs a voice.

Name one with --voice, for example:

  FlashTerm deck.txt --generate-audio --voice fr_FR-siwis-medium

Or name the synthesiser yourself with FLASHTERM_TTS_RENDER, where {out} is
the file to write and the text arrives on standard input:

  FLASHTERM_TTS_RENDER="espeak-ng -v fr --stdin -w {out}"

There is no default because a voice implies a language, and guessing it would
render a French deck in English.

